From: tinker-edge-r-debian
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: rk817: fix the right microphone boost bits

RK817_CODEC_AMIC_CFG0 holds the boost of both microphone amplifiers: bits 3 and 2
for the left one, bits 1 and 0 for the right one (the vendor driver writes 0x0f to
enable both). "Mic Boost R1" and "Mic Boost R2" pointed at bit 3, the left boost,
so the right amplifier never got its boost. On the ASUS Tinker Edge R the headset
microphone of the 3.5 mm jack arrives in the right channel: its level rises by
about 30 dB with the right bits (measured on the board).

Signed-off-by: tinker-edge-r-debian
---
--- a/sound/soc/codecs/rk817_codec.c
+++ b/sound/soc/codecs/rk817_codec.c
@@ -136,8 +136,8 @@
 	/* capture path R */
 	SND_SOC_DAPM_ADC("ADC R", "Capture", RK817_CODEC_AADC_CFG0, 6, 1),
 	SND_SOC_DAPM_SUPPLY("PGA R Power On", RK817_CODEC_AMIC_CFG0, 4, 1, NULL, 0),
-	SND_SOC_DAPM_SUPPLY("Mic Boost R1", RK817_CODEC_AMIC_CFG0, 3, 0, NULL, 0),
-	SND_SOC_DAPM_SUPPLY("Mic Boost R2", RK817_CODEC_AMIC_CFG0, 3, 0, NULL, 0),
+	SND_SOC_DAPM_SUPPLY("Mic Boost R1", RK817_CODEC_AMIC_CFG0, 1, 0, NULL, 0),
+	SND_SOC_DAPM_SUPPLY("Mic Boost R2", RK817_CODEC_AMIC_CFG0, 0, 0, NULL, 0),
 
 	/* playback path common */
 	SND_SOC_DAPM_SUPPLY("DAC Clock", RK817_CODEC_DTOP_DIGEN_CLKE, 3, 0, NULL, 0),
